     No Sound in Windows – Raw Notes

Check Volume and Mute Settings
- Ensure Windows is not muted  
- Increase system volume  
- Verify speakers/headphones are not muted  

Test Audio Output Device
- Click speaker icon in taskbar  
- Change audio output device  
- Toggle through available devices until sound is heard  

Test Speakers or Headphones
- Try different headset or speakers  
- Confirm external speakers are powered on  

        Check Cable Connections
- Ensure audio cables are securely connected  
- On PC: plug into green audio jack  
- Use front or rear port with headphone icon  

      Audio Driver Issues
Drivers allow Windows to communicate with hardware.  
Missing, corrupted, or incorrect drivers can result in no sound.

          Check Drivers
- Open Device Manager  
- Expand **Sound, video and game controllers**  
- Right-click audio device: Properties  
- Check device status for errors  
- *(Reference: Screenshot1 )*  

        Fix Driver Problems
- Right-click device: Update driver  
- If Windows cannot find a driver:
  - Download manually from manufacturer  

        Driver Sources
- Laptop / Prebuilt PC - Search using PC model number  
- Custom PC: Search using motherboard model (onboard audio)  
- Specialized headset/speakers - Search using device model number  

        No Audio Device Detected
Possible causes:
- Audio device not detected  
- Faulty or missing driver  
- Onboard audio disabled in BIOS  

          BIOS Check (Advanced)
- Verify onboard audio is enabled in BIOS settings
